   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "The numerator x - 7 has limit 0 as x approaches 7, and the denominator sqrt(x + 2) - 3 has limit sqrt(9) - 3 = 0, so the form is zero over zero.",
         "mathjson": 0
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "Multiply numerator and denominator by sqrt(x + 2) + 3. The denominator becomes (x + 2) - 9 = x - 7, so the quotient is (x - 7)(sqrt(x + 2) + 3)/(x - 7).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Divide",
